# Entity view and edit

## Pattern

Users with write permission edit **on the same surface** they view — not a separate mystery route.

| Surface | View | Edit |
|---------|------|------|
| Detail page (`/inventory/[sku]`) | Default | `?edit=1` or **Szerkesztés** toggles `ProductEditPanel` in `ProductDetailShell` |
| List row sheet (`DataTable` `rowDetail`) | Quick summary | **Szerkesztés** replaces sheet body with `ProductEditPanel` (no nested `EntitySheet`) |
| Create | — | Dedicated `/new` route only |

## Shared pieces

- `ProductEditPanel` — loads `getProductEditContext`, renders `ProductEditForm`.
- `ProductEditForm` — single form; optional `onCancel` for inline edit flows.

## Do not

- Add parallel `/entity/[id]/edit` pages unless redirecting to `?edit=1` for bookmarks.
- Open a second `EntitySheet` for edit when the parent already provides one.
- Split BOM edit from product edit — BOM is a section in `ProductEditForm` (`ComponentLinesEditor`).

## BOM component lines

`ComponentLinesEditor` shows **name + CRM SKU** (`productName` + `productSku`). Populate `productName` when loading existing lines from the server.

## Product SKU display

Any user-visible CRM SKU must include the product name — see `.cursor/rules/product-sku-display.mdc` (`ProductSkuLabel`, `formatProductSkuLine`).
